---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import release from "../../../data/release.json";

const issuesUrl = "https://github.com/devjoe/devjoe-garmin-site/issues";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Support — Burnished Sky Ahead"
  description="Troubleshooting, support, and feedback for Burnished Sky Ahead."
  current="support"
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Burnished Sky Ahead</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">Start with the quick checks below. If the problem remains, share only the details needed to reproduce it.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="callout language-callout">
      <p><strong>台灣使用者：</strong><a href="/zh-tw/burnished-sky-ahead/support/">前往繁體中文台灣支持頁</a>。</p>
    </div>
    <section class="content-grid">
      <aside>Quick checks</aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>A setting is missing on my watch</h2>
        <p>Options depend on the model. <a href="/burnished-sky-ahead/devices/">Find your watch in the feature comparison</a> to check weekly swim, wind signals, Chinese weather and long-press controls. Confirm that Connect IQ shows version {release.product.version} for the watch you’re configuring.</p>
        <h2>Watch face cannot load</h2>
        <p>A brief IQ! has been observed on Forerunner 970 during some updates. Leave the watch face and return once. If it persists, try the steps below and report your model, firmware and version; repeated IQ! errors should not be ignored.</p>
        <p>If the preparing or restoring screen persists, or recovery steps appear:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Select a built-in Garmin watch face.</li>
          <li>Enter and exit always-on display (AOD). On Forerunner 970, use the LIGHT button.</li>
          <li>Switch back to Burnished Sky Ahead.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>If the problem remains, include the device model, firmware, and watch-face version in your report below.</p>
        <h2>Weather looks stale</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Garmin’s Weather app and confirm its current data.</li>
          <li>Sync Garmin Connect and allow Garmin’s cached weather time to refresh.</li>
          <li>Confirm the watch face has its requested permissions.</li>
          <li>Restart the watch if settings or cached data remain stale.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          The watch face shows the current condition caption directly. It does
          not reveal coordinates or rotate through a provider/location label.
        </p>
        <h2>Read the lower-left forecast</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The three small labels are local clock hours, not “hours from now.”</li>
          <li>Each value belongs to the forecast node beside it.</li>
          <li>RAIN, SNOW, and MIX show precipitation chance; TEMP shows forecast temperature.</li>
          <li>The icon identifies the selected forecast mode. Missing data remains <code>--</code>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/burnished-sky-ahead/forecast/">See the visual three-node forecast guide.</a></p>
        <p>On supported touch watches, long-press the lower-left forecast to switch back to temperature when rain chance is shown.</p>
        <h2>Show or hide your Widget</h2>
        <p>On supported touch watches, enable "Hold Widget to show / hide" in settings, then long-press the left Widget area. Long-press the same area to show it again.</p>
        <p>Choose Countdown, Days since, Analog or Digital second time zones separately for day and night. Widget names support English letters and selected symbols.</p>
        <h2>Status rail</h2>
        <p>
          On supported devices, compact icons beside the time show alarm and Do
          Not Disturb state when Garmin reports them. Connect IQ does not expose
          the next alarm time, repeat rule, weekday, or Smart Wake state, so the
          watch face does not guess them. Status indicators stay hidden in AOD.
        </p>
        <p>
          Show notification count is Off by default. When enabled, the rail
          shows Garmin's on-device notification count, capped at <code>99+</code>.
          It does not read message contents, sender names, or notification text.
        </p>
        <h2>Settings</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>AOD ornament:</strong> Three-rail, Victory Laurel, Quoted Time, None, or Daily Rotation.</li>
          <li><strong>Weather frame:</strong> Faceted Seal, Simple Circle, or None.</li>
          <li><strong>Outdoor Brief:</strong> Off, Always on, Toggle by long press, or Smart on supported AMOLED watches.</li>
          <li><strong>Weather Signals:</strong> Off or On on AMOLED watches, and strong-wind signals on selected MIP watches.</li>
          <li><strong>Weather and weekday language:</strong> English or Traditional Chinese; English by default. The numeric date stays unchanged.</li>
          <li><strong>Show notification count:</strong> Off or On; Off by default.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Choose two custom data fields, plus separate day and night color themes and Widgets. Field choices vary by watch.</p>
        <h2>Weekly swim distance</h2>
        <p>On supported models, choose “Weekly swim (on watch)” for either custom field. It uses swimming activities saved on this watch and your watch’s week-start setting. It is not the full Garmin Connect account total.</p>
        <p>A valid week with no saved swimming shows 0; unavailable or incomplete history shows <code>--</code>. Real pool, open-water and multisport feedback is still welcome. Include the watch model and expected weekly distance, without posting private activity files or locations.</p>
        <h2>Wind direction</h2>
        <p>The arrow shows where the wind is blowing to, with north at the top of the watch. NOW uses current weather; LATER uses the selected forecast. On MIP, Weather Signals covers strong wind only and is available on selected models.</p>
        <h2>Report a problem</h2>
        <p>
          Include the device model, firmware, Burnished Sky Ahead version,
          expected behavior, visible fallback text, and whether it occurs in
          active mode, AOD, or both.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Keep public reports private-safe.</strong> Do not post precise coordinates, account data, payment details, or private Garmin logs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a class="button primary" href={`${issuesUrl}/new/choose`}>Open a public issue</a>
          <a class="button" href={`mailto:${release.urls.supportEmail}`}>Email private support</a>
        </div>
        <h2>Optional support</h2>
        <p>
          Burnished Sky Ahead is free. {release.support.purpose}
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Tips are voluntary.</strong> They do not purchase, unlock, or guarantee any feature, product, service, or release date. </p>
        </div>
        {release.support.url ? (
          <div class="action-row">
            <a class="button" href={release.support.url}>Leave a tip on Ko-fi</a>
            <a class="button" href="/burnished-sky-ahead/roadmap/">See what’s new</a>
          </div>
        ) : (
          <p class="status-tag">Tip link will be published at launch</p>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
